  "scope": "C301 fresh bounded8..32-byte noncryptographic rejection hash based on hardware AES round mixing.8..16 use two exact8-byte endpoint loads covering every byte;17..32 use first/last16-byte blocks covering every byte; length enters fixed data-independent seed. Two final diffusion rounds follow payload absorption, full64 folded result then existing0/1 adjustment. Other lengths or architectures retain original std::hash. ARM AESE+AESMC+XOR implements x86 AESENC round semantics; native macro checked, no new march flags. This is NOT AES encryption, authentication, cryptographic/universal hash guarantee or an imported library/competitor implementation. Full key length/every byte comparison remains final identity for all collisions; owner routing/private8-byte table/arena/countries/parser/events/PGO unchanged. Unlike271 scalar multiply/rotate and279 scalar short-word mix, new primitive uses nonlinear hardware rounds. Native public1/6/12/fourfull screen first; independent scalar AES-round/vector/all-byte/guard/collision/native-GCC-AES-fallback/main/untrained/race/image/default/actual proof before promotion.",
